To connect to the Polars MCP server, you need to refer to the documentation of your preferred client. The installation instructions for the MCP server are provided in the `!!! note "MCP server installation"` section of the user guide. 

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "ask_polars": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["mcp-remote", "https://mcp.pola.rs/mcp"]
    }
  }
}
```

Source: user-guide/misc/polars_llms.md > Polars MCP server

A good resource for learning how to write a Polars plugin is the [Polars plugins tutorial](https://marcogorelli.github.io/polars-plugins-tutorial/). This tutorial provides minimal and simple examples to help you get started. 

```python
# Example from the Polars plugins tutorial
import polars as pl

df = pl.DataFrame({"A": [1, 2, 3], "B": [4, 5, 6]})

class MyPlugin(pl.Plugin):
    def __init__(self):
        pass

    def execute(self, df):
        return df.with_column(pl.col("A") + pl.col("B"))

MyPlugin().execute(df)
```

Source: [Polars plugins tutorial](https://marcogorelli.github.io/polars-plugins-tutorial/)
